# Use-case 10 gap 6 (claim C4, loud half) -- FIXED 2026-08-26 by the
# template-clone isolation change (ADR-005): the include+alias
# combination no longer derails id(key(0)). Historically a leaked
# type mark froze the pending key(0) (the marked-func freeze), so
# id() saw the unevaluated call and refused it with a bogus
# [aontu/id_name]. Spread applications are now full per-destination
# instances and references defer on pending mark wrappers, so the
# spread's key(0) resolves per record and id() names each entity.
# Pinned in both engines: test/spec/file.tsv load-alias-idspread.
# expected: {"customers":{"c1":{"ledgerId":5}},"schema":{}} exit 0
# actual:   {"customers":{"c1":{"ledgerId":5}},"schema":{}} exit 0
@"./alias-vocab.aon"
customers: { &: id(key(0)) & $.schema.C }
customers: c1: { ledgerId: 5 }
